{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791130064,"nonce":"i+B0l2EaQvHzeNHXOnkzk6WlX9s=","title":"A Cast from f64 to f64 reaches a native call as integer bits","message":"A TypedExpression::Cast whose source and target are both F64 lowers to an HIR bitcast %p0 (f64 -\u003e f64). Passed on to an extern f64 parameter, the callee received the integer conversion of the value reinterpreted as f64 bits (3.0 arrived as 1.5e-323, the bits of the integer 3), in both the interpreter and Cranelift (ZYNTAX_BASELINE_THRESHOLD=1). Seen while building native host bindings; the bindings now skip a cast whose types already match, so nothing depends on it, but the cast itself is wrong. Reproduce: a generated function f(p0: f64) whose body calls an extern g(f64) with Cast(p0, F64).","files":null}]}